WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.360
- All right, Stephen

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.920
Stephen, where'd you grow up?

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.220
Where you from originally?

00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:08.860
- I grew up over

00:00:10.359 --> 00:00:11.963
in the Alhambra area,

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:13.700
not too far from here.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.810
- Suburb of L.A.?

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:15.960
- Yeah.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:17.547
- And, tell me about your
childhood, you grow up

00:00:17.547 --> 00:00:19.965
with both your parents?

00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:21.193
- No,

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.600
early divorce,

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.740
I was like five years old or so.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:28.573
- Your parents split up?

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:30.570
- Yeah, I was with my dad

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.860
for most of my childhood
and that was really cool,

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.410
then I went over to my
mom for a little bit.

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:40.469
And then she moved so now I'm
actually out here on my own.

00:00:40.469 --> 00:00:42.623
- How long you been out here on Skid Row?

00:00:42.623 --> 00:00:45.460
- About two and a half, three years maybe.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:46.300
I try not to

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.240
hang out here as much as I can,

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.370
'cause I know it's crazy and dangerous.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.418
- Yeah, it is.

00:00:53.418 --> 00:00:56.760
- I'd like to have a life
where it's progressing,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.317
but I know drugs,

00:00:59.317 --> 00:01:01.813
it's like you can't move too far.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.543
- How was your childhood?

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.690
- Fortunately it was good.
The divorce, I was young

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:12.143
enough where it, I didn't know

00:01:12.143 --> 00:01:14.980
what relationships were
like so it didn't know.

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:16.723
It really didn't have an effect.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:23.240
I still saw Mom and Dad,
they weren't together,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.210
I just didn't see the relationship because

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.093
I was too young to understand
what a relationship was.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.734
So, I mean, it was good.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:34.150
My father was a good guy.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.520
He took care of me a lot.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.893
My mom was a good mother.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.060
I don't have any siblings but it was cool.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.230
It was fine.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:45.777
- Then when you were on
your own, where'd you go?

00:01:47.382 --> 00:01:48.380
Did you go to college?

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.930
- Well, I attempted that
but I was never really

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:51.763
into academics.

00:01:51.763 --> 00:01:52.596
- Yeah

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:56.760
- That was at the same point in time where

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.760
I started using drugs so
that was the critical pivot.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.920
Do I try to do the
academics and do that route

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.920
or I wasn't going to say drugs were going

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.420
to be a route of life
but that's kinda like

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.970
what took over and became life.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.784
And, that's what ended up happening.

00:02:14.784 --> 00:02:17.733
- What were the first drugs
you played around with?

00:02:20.199 --> 00:02:22.730
- It was like marijuana and drinking

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.460
and then Vicodin pills
were very cool thing

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.460
to do at the time. You progress with those

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.950
and then sure enough injuries happen.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:38.650
You get on pills again
and then they give you

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.820
a little stronger ones and
those things get harder to get.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:44.390
And then you just kinda jump
over to opiates or heroin.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.700
- Prescription runs out and you

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.497
- Yeah, exactly, prescription goes

00:02:47.497 --> 00:02:50.420
and street price is expensive.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.768
Doctors won't give you anything.

00:02:51.768 --> 00:02:52.883
- That's a common way.

00:02:52.883 --> 00:02:55.000
People get addicted.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:55.833
- Yeah

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:58.520
- And, so where are you staying now?

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.120
- I used to have a tent around here.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.769
I've been on the train quite a bit though.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:06.460
I want to get out of the area.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.293
I really do.

00:03:07.293 --> 00:03:10.860
So I tell myself to
get on the train to go.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.733
I get on it and then I go

00:03:11.733 --> 00:03:13.080
then I realize oh fuck,

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:14.359
I'm going to be sick.

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:15.192
- Yeah

00:03:15.192 --> 00:03:16.170
- So I gotta come back.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.300
- You gotta come back to get your heroin.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.133
- Yeah

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:22.263
- What do you do for money now?

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:25.930
- It was boosting.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:26.956
I don't do that anymore.

00:03:26.956 --> 00:03:30.530
So now I just try to find little stores

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:34.740
and I try to sweep their parking lot

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.200
or do some windows, something.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.389
Random, different stores I know.

00:03:38.389 --> 00:03:40.970
They'll help out, like
20 bucks here and there.

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:41.803
- Nice

00:03:41.803 --> 00:03:42.636
- Yeah

00:03:42.636 --> 00:03:43.655
- Something honest.

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:45.550
- I don't want to go to jail, man,

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.717
I don't, I don't

00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:48.500
- Have you been in jail?

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:50.180
- Yeah, I'm tired of it dude.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.800
I'm too old for it.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.130
The time is not worth the
money you get for stealing.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:56.815
It's stupid.

00:03:56.815 --> 00:03:57.648
- Yeah

00:03:57.648 --> 00:03:59.283
- I try and find the honest work.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.820
I can find a job,

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:02.653
an actual job

00:04:02.653 --> 00:04:04.370
paying job with a check and stuff

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:06.633
but residence,

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:08.950
The Refresh Spot's cool.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:10.480
It keeps you clean, you
can shower and stuff

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:11.850
but sometimes it's so crowded that

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.509
you miss your showers there.

00:04:15.509 --> 00:04:17.150
- For those who don't know,

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:18.756
there's a place called The Refresh Spot

00:04:18.756 --> 00:04:21.255
down here where people
can take showers and

00:04:21.255 --> 00:04:23.470
what else do you do over there?

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:24.390
- You can do laundry,

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.793
charge your phone if you have one.

00:04:25.793 --> 00:04:28.224
Sometimes they give you referrals or

00:04:28.224 --> 00:04:30.774
different other resources around the area.

00:04:30.774 --> 00:04:33.688
- There's really resources
for everything and anything,

00:04:33.688 --> 00:04:34.521
right?

00:04:34.521 --> 00:04:35.354
- Yeah, there is down here

00:04:35.354 --> 00:04:38.611
- Food, clothing, rehab, recovery, shoes.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.660
The only thing they don't seem to give out

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.493
are tents, right?

00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:42.873
- Time and time, some places do.

00:04:42.873 --> 00:04:43.903
- Do they?

00:04:43.903 --> 00:04:45.980
But, I notice with the
clothes and stuff like that

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.043
you have to hit 'em on a good day or

00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:50.920
the place themselves are gonna take it and

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.681
give it to their residents there.

00:04:53.681 --> 00:04:54.514
- Yeah

00:04:54.514 --> 00:04:56.346
Did you ever have dreams
of doing something

00:04:56.346 --> 00:04:58.313
in your life, or goals?

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.910
- A specific dream, like a career dream or

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:04.743
just like something

00:05:04.743 --> 00:05:05.938
- No, no, no like goals.

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:07.370
I mean like did you
want to become a doctor

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:10.923
or a lawyer or anything like that.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:14.003
- I mean every kid is like
oh I want to be a doctor

00:05:14.003 --> 00:05:16.030
or I want to be a police
officer or something like that.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:16.990
I did too, you know?

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:18.160
I did.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.820
But I never followed through with it.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:21.713
Right now,

00:05:23.830 --> 00:05:25.760
I could say I'm still in that same place.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.500
I have these goals.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.690
I know what I want to do in a sense but

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:31.620
it's the first steps,

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.118
I don't know how to do it.

00:05:33.118 --> 00:05:36.332
How do I go about getting
to those positions?

00:05:36.332 --> 00:05:39.897
I know how to enroll in
school and you do that.

00:05:39.897 --> 00:05:43.450
I know how to show up and be on time but

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:47.680
after that, where does it take me?

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.630
If I want to go to the
construction sites and

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:52.127
say "Hey, you guys hiring?",

00:05:52.127 --> 00:05:53.881
"No, we're not right
now. Go to our website."

00:05:53.881 --> 00:05:57.890
Do that and keep showing
up and it's still "no",

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.684
then I don't know what to do there.

00:05:59.684 --> 00:06:01.970
I don't know how to expand that.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.623
My networking skills aren't that great.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:08.900
- And then, your drug is heroin?

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:10.070
- Yeah.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.930
Sometimes crystal meth too.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:13.950
- And being addicted to heroin or meth,

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:16.820
you can't really make it
through a full work day, right?

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:18.483
- No, well,

00:06:18.483 --> 00:06:20.910
I can make it through a full work day

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:23.520
but it's making sure I have something

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.820
in the morning to start
that day is the issue.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.593
Having enough money in
the morning to go to work.

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:33.263
After that it's fine.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.890
Like say if I start a job,

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:38.812
it's gonna take two weeks
before I start getting

00:06:38.812 --> 00:06:41.620
my first check so what am I going to do

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.470
the first two weeks?

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:44.550
I have to really try to make sure I don't

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.980
get in trouble by the law

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.646
or I have to make sure I have enough

00:06:49.646 --> 00:06:51.693
to continue to go to work.

00:06:52.905 --> 00:06:55.963
So it has to be really planned out.

00:06:57.353 --> 00:06:58.800
And, out here, things never go

00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.900
the way they're supposed to.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:01.073
- Never

00:07:01.073 --> 00:07:01.906
- Yeah

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.170
- If someone was to walk
you over to one of the

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:07.177
recovery programs here and just like

00:07:07.177 --> 00:07:09.747
dropped you off and
say "stick with it" and

00:07:09.747 --> 00:07:12.787
"follow through", "get
your life in order", and

00:07:12.787 --> 00:07:15.670
"get out of this
neighborhood", and "get a job",

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:16.503
and "get your life together",

00:07:16.503 --> 00:07:18.043
do you think that would work out?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:24.003
- Yeah, I mean, I do and I don't.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.070
I want that.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.880
I want to be in recovery.

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:30.020
I want to be sober, I do.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.341
But, I also want to have freedoms too.

00:07:32.341 --> 00:07:34.730
I don't wanna have to be bound to

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.950
six seven groups a day,

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:39.374
which takes up all day and

00:07:39.374 --> 00:07:41.900
they say you can't get a job until

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:44.200
you are six months into it.

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:46.150
Well shit.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.900
I mean I know that's not
any kind of amount of time.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.980
Six months is nothing looking at it.

00:07:50.980 --> 00:07:53.370
But in that moment, sitting there,

00:07:53.370 --> 00:07:55.200
you're like "damn, well,
I wanted to do that now."

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.060
And, it's just that whole
"I want it now" thing.

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:59.970
It cuts it off, blocks it out of the way.

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:00.803
- Yeah

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.540
- I would do it right now, I would,

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:05.373
I want to

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.980
I guess the uncertainty of the future too.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:12.730
- Do you think some of this is just

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:17.450
your self-worth is being what it is,

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.730
it kinda just like puts
you in this situation

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.852
and you almost feel like somewhere,

00:08:21.852 --> 00:08:23.420
subconsciously you deserve it?

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.200
That this is where you belong
or something like that?

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.385
- I used to think that way

00:08:26.385 --> 00:08:27.540
I used to

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:33.550
It was like that for a
majority of my addiction.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:38.100
It wasn't 'til recently that,

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.550
I want to say within the last

00:08:40.611 --> 00:08:43.350
I think it was actually getting down here

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:47.720
they actually made me
feel I had more self-worth

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.301
because I actually saw
the rawness of this.

00:08:51.301 --> 00:08:52.134
- Yeah

00:08:52.134 --> 00:08:54.260
- And actually, it's
kinda messed up to say,

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:55.093
but it actually kinda

00:08:55.093 --> 00:08:56.623
boosted my self-esteem almost.

00:08:57.779 --> 00:08:58.612
- Yeah?

00:08:59.908 --> 00:09:02.540
- But I know it's not for everyone.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.060
It doesn't happen for everyone.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.710
Who's to say it's gonna last too?

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:08.670
Who's to say it's gonna last?

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:09.503
- Yeah

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.700
This is the bottom of the barrel.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.960
- Yeah and I know like some people say

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.271
they get down here,

00:09:18.271 --> 00:09:20.691
they get off the bus and they never leave.

00:09:20.691 --> 00:09:24.030
That's kinda so far what's
happened to me in a sense.

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:25.930
- The Greyhound Station is
right at the end of the,

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:27.400
you see it from here.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.860
That's where people come
from all over the country

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:30.095
and get dropped off and

00:09:30.095 --> 00:09:31.589
- Think they're gonna go
to the financial district

00:09:31.589 --> 00:09:34.363
- (laughs) They go through (garbled).

00:09:34.363 --> 00:09:36.830
- Yeah, they can't make it the half mile.

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.913
- They spend the rest of their lives here.

00:09:40.842 --> 00:09:42.443
I hope you don't.

00:09:42.443 --> 00:09:44.140
- No, I don't want that man, I don't.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.230
- How old are you?

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:46.170
- 27

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:47.003
- 27

00:09:47.003 --> 00:09:47.836
- Yeah

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.600
- Well Stephen, thank
you for talking to me and

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:53.433
- Yeah, no problem.

00:09:53.433 --> 00:09:55.973
- good luck and I hope
you figure out a way to

00:09:55.973 --> 00:09:57.880
climb out of this.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:09:59.613
- Yeah,

00:10:03.059 --> 00:10:06.960
I need to sit down and
really like thoroughly

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:07.793
just

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:10.820
think it through or just

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:15.243
find out how to go about it.

00:10:15.243 --> 00:10:17.360
The resources are here, just use 'em.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:18.490
That's what I gotta do just

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:19.804
fucking use them things.

00:10:19.804 --> 00:10:21.366
- Yeah

00:10:21.366 --> 00:10:22.707
- That's what it comes down to.

00:10:22.707 --> 00:10:25.493
Half measures or whole steps.

00:10:26.690 --> 00:10:27.523
- That's it.

00:10:27.523 --> 00:10:28.539
- Yeah

00:10:28.539 --> 00:10:29.910
- All right, well, thank
you for talking to me.

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:30.743
- Awesome brother

00:10:30.743 --> 00:10:31.576
- Thank you man.

00:10:31.576 --> 00:10:32.409
- Cool.

